"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"hyperedge, once, with no self-loops. Edges ascend by (index of u, index of v), u the lower."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Singletons and empty hyperedges add no edge. Lossy and quadratic: one hyperedge of k members"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is k(k − 1)\/2 edges."}]},"doc://GraphProtocols/documentation/GraphProtocols/BidirectionalDirectedGraph":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/BidirectionalDirectedGraph","url":"\/documentation\/graphprotocols\/bidirectionaldirectedgraph","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"protocol"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P6VertexQa","text":"Vertex"},{"kind":"text","text":"> : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols08DirectedA0P","text":"DirectedGraph"}],"title":"BidirectionalDirectedGraph","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A directed graph that also answers in-neighborhoods: Boost’s "},{"code":"BidirectionalGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":". Kept apart"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from "},{"code":"DirectedGraph","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" because in-adjacency usually costs extra storage, and many algorithms only"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"go forward."}]},"doc://Hypergraphs/documentation/Hypergraphs/GraphProtocols/Hypergraph/rank":{"role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","title":"rank","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The greatest hyperedge size (Berge’s rank), 0 with no hyperedges. O(m)."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/Hypergraphs\/documentation\/Hypergraphs\/GraphProtocols\/Hypergraph\/rank","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"var"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"rank"},{"kind"